From 87a608fb60c41736ca7af0eaef0ceadbabb7bb5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LightCraft additional extensions <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Quick Retouch tools in Develop: Dodge, Burn, Sponge,
 Quick / Object Selection, Clone Stamp, Quick Mask

Photoshop-style retouch tools built only from existing commands (UI-only; no engine, pipeline or
GPU change). A new Quick Retouch row tops the Masking panel, the commands are in Window > Tools,
and the default keymap gains Shift+B (cycle Dodge/Burn/Sponge), Shift+W (cycle Quick/Object
Selection), Shift+Q (Clone Stamp) and Q (Quick Mask), all previously unbound.

- Dodge / Burn: a new brush mask with local Exposure +/-(2 EV x Exposure %), intersected with a
  Luminance Range for Shadows / Midtones / Highlights (All: none); every other local slider zeroed
  so a remembered brush effect does not mix in. One undo step (begin/endInteraction).
- Sponge: a new brush mask with local Saturation -/+ Flow % (Desaturate / Saturate).
- Options bar: Range, Exposure %, Mode, Flow edit the mask in use (one undo step each).
- Quick Selection: an empty brush mask, Auto Mask on, a larger brush, the overlay shown; Auto
  Mask and size come back when the tool is left.
- Object Selection: the existing SAM 3 Object mask (start_object, with its download offer).
- Clone Stamp: Remove panel in Clone mode; Alt/Option-click sets the source (spot.add source),
  with an Aligned option.
- Quick Mask: red 50 % colour overlay with the brush; the previous overlay settings come back.

Simplified and Traditional Chinese strings; headless tests in tests/retouch_tools.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
